 "text": "## Win Rate by Segment\n\n**Mid-Market is the clear sweet spot** \u2014 44% win rate, nearly 2x Enterprise and double SMB. However, Enterprise deals drive the most total ARR despite a lower win rate.\n\n| Segment | Opportunities | Won | Win Rate | Avg Deal Size | Total Won ARR |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Mid-Market** | 48 | 21 | **43.8%** | $41K | $868K |\n| **Enterprise** | 53 | 17 | **32.1%** | $137K | $2.3M |\n| **SMB** | 9 | 2 | **22.2%** | $5K | $9K |\n\n### Key Takeaways\n\n- **Mid-Market** is the most winnable segment \u2014 invest here for volume and efficiency. At $41K avg deal size, it balances scale with close-ability.\n- **Enterprise** generates the most revenue ($2.3M won ARR) despite a lower win rate. Improving Enterprise win rate by even 5 pts would yield ~$685K in additional ARR.\n- **SMB** has both the lowest win rate and smallest deal size \u2014 with only 9 opportunities it's likely under-resourced, but the economics are challenging given the $5K avg ACV.\n\n### Recommendation\nSales should **prioritize Mid-Market** for reliable quota attainment, while selectively investing in Enterprise deals where there's strong qualification (budget, champion, clear timeline). SMB is best served via a PLG/low-touch motion rather than direct sales effort.",
